WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:06.340
May I ask if anyone among us

2
00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:08.989
has the future aspiration

3
00:00:08.990 --> 00:00:10.890
of becoming a gangster?

4
00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:21.190
Of course not, right?

5
00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:23.039
Although it's true

6
00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:27.109
there must be a few cases of individuals who have gone astray,

7
00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:28.620
but our school

8
00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:32.089
has become like a training ground for gangsters.

9
00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:34.999
Someone submitted a petition to the Ministry of Education.

10
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.510
- What the... - Ah, what the hell, damn it...

11
00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:40.810
Therefore, our school

12
00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:44.440
not only suffered a huge blow to its public image,

13
00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:48.230
but we've also been notified that the Ministry of Education will send an inspection team.

14
00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:50.679
Unfortunately,

15
00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:53.770
this is a major issue that could likely lead to the school's closure.

16
00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:57.690
Isn't that right, Teacher Lee Han-kyung?

17
00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:05.360
Well?

18
00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:08.740
Do you want to come up to the podium and say a few words?

19
00:01:09.650 --> 00:01:12.319
To the students who were suddenly stigmatized as a gangster school

20
00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:14.930
and took the blame.

21
00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:18.209
At least apologize, saying sorry

22
00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:19.330
is the most basic principle

23
00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:21.970
as an educator, isn't it?

24
00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:23.670
Hurry up.

25
00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:26.910
- Come on out. - Come out quickly.

26
00:01:33.230 --> 00:01:34.339
Hurry up.

27
00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:35.659
Hurry to the stage.

28
00:01:35.660 --> 00:01:37.260
Go quickly.

29
00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:22.710
Our school

30
00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:26.620
is not normal right now.

31
00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:29.199
- Calling it abnormal... - What's not normal?

32
00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:32.290
Although I haven't been working at this school for long,

33
00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:34.590
I've been observing it for a long time.

34
00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:37.500
Through my mentor,

35
00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:42.210
the late Teacher Woo Jung-hwa.

36
00:02:43.940 --> 00:02:44.800
What?

37
00:02:55.330 --> 00:02:57.659
(1 year ago)

38
00:02:57.660 --> 00:02:59.160
So you aren't busy.

39
00:03:01.130 --> 00:03:03.590
Still have time to celebrate your teacher's birthday.

40
00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:06.670
Can you pass the recruitment exam being this relaxed?

41
00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:08.000
Of course.

42
00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:10.309
- 'Of course'? - Yeah.

43
00:03:10.310 --> 00:03:11.579
- 'Of course'? - What's wrong?

44
00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:12.809
- Wow. - What's wrong?

45
00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:14.099
- What is it? What's wrong... - Lee Han-kyung said

46
00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:15.670
- What is it now... - 'Of course'?

47
00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:19.080
Ugh, seriously.

48
00:03:19.910 --> 00:03:22.039
Why did you keep this?

49
00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:23.529
Delete it.

50
00:03:23.530 --> 00:03:25.410
Wow, seriously.

51
00:03:26.540 --> 00:03:27.540
It's really amazing, isn't it?

52
00:03:27.541 --> 00:03:30.540
That a person can change so much.

53
00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:35.850
But seeing you gives me strength.

54
00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:42.200
You must be very tired.

55
00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:44.530
It's just...

56
00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:48.590
the kids are not what I expected.

57
00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:53.710
That's why I'm asking, why did you have to go to that kind of school?

58
00:03:56.280 --> 00:03:57.409
But,

59
00:03:57.410 --> 00:03:59.089
because you are there, Teacher,

60
00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:00.090
they will change.

61
00:04:00.520 --> 00:04:01.380
Just like I did.

62
00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:04.319
You just focus on doing your own thing well.

63
00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:06.500
If you don't pass the recruitment exam, don't contact me again.

64
00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:09.510
I understand.

65
00:04:10.110 --> 00:04:12.350
I will also think about that.

66
00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:13.870
What?

67
00:04:15.010 --> 00:04:18.070
Come on, a toast to Lee Han-kyung passing the recruitment exam!

68
00:04:23.410 --> 00:04:25.449
In an alley in the East District of Ancheon,

69
00:04:25.450 --> 00:04:27.419
an incident occurred where a woman in her 40s

70
00:04:27.420 --> 00:04:29.710
was fatally stabbed with a weapon.

71
00:04:30.340 --> 00:04:31.519
The police believe

72
00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:33.219
this case is a random killing

73
00:04:33.220 --> 00:04:34.590
and are continuing their investigation.

74
00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:41.240
I will make this school

75
00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:44.120
return to normal.

76
00:04:44.830 --> 00:04:46.520
- Teacher. - If, up until now,

77
00:04:47.070 --> 00:04:50.490
efforts were made to change the people trying to ruin the school,

78
00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:53.449
now I will protect those

79
00:04:53.450 --> 00:04:55.870
students who have been hurt by them.

80
00:04:58.050 --> 00:05:00.110
I don't care who they are.

81
00:05:06.010 --> 00:05:07.240
What the...

82
00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:26.270
Being hit hurts, right?

83
00:05:27.580 --> 00:05:29.030
You are also a normal person.

84
00:05:29.780 --> 00:05:31.310
So enough with the arrogance.

85
00:05:37.950 --> 00:05:41.219
(3rd Period: English - Singular Form)

86
00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:42.290
(National Language. 3rd Period: English - Singular Form. Math.)

87
00:05:49.030 --> 00:05:51.169
(Those who want to study, gather around!)

88
00:05:51.170 --> 00:05:53.340
(Hwang Min-hyun)

89
00:05:53.770 --> 00:05:55.309
(Han Ji-eun)

90
00:05:55.310 --> 00:05:56.940
(Cha Woo-min)

91
00:06:06.780 --> 00:06:08.279
(Lee Jong-hyun)

92
00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:09.490
(Shin Soo-hyun)

93
00:06:10.450 --> 00:06:12.860
(Yoon Sang-jeong, Gong Do-yu)

94
00:06:18.330 --> 00:06:23.000
"Study Group"

95
00:06:23.380 --> 00:06:25.099
Wow, damn it.

96
00:06:25.100 --> 00:06:26.869
Wow, isn't that absolutely crazy?

97
00:06:26.870 --> 00:06:28.429
Wow, he actually punched Pi Han-wool.

98
00:06:28.430 --> 00:06:30.030
- Hey, hey, hey. - Damn it.

99
00:06:31.250 --> 00:06:32.519
Is senior Pi Han-wool your friend?

100
00:06:32.520 --> 00:06:34.739
You really need to be careful or you're dead, idiot.

101
00:06:34.740 --> 00:06:35.899
Hey, nobody is listening.

102
00:06:35.900 --> 00:06:37.719
Ever since we were in the auditorium, everyone's been talking about Pi Han-wool, Pi Han-wool.

103
00:06:37.720 --> 00:06:38.600
- Be quiet. - Ah, but,

104
00:06:38.601 --> 00:06:40.219
people saying that kid Yoon Jiamin is a monster,

105
00:06:40.220 --> 00:06:42.169
he really is a total monster.

106
00:06:42.170 --> 00:06:43.189
How could he punch Pi Han-wool?

107
00:06:43.190 --> 00:06:44.210
Hey.

108
00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:55.349
Can you still study those vocabulary cards in this situation?

109
00:06:55.350 --> 00:06:58.200
Right now, not only are we not family or whatever,
we're about to be kicked out of the standing army too.

110
00:06:58.640 --> 00:07:00.280
Is that important?

111
00:07:00.750 --> 00:07:02.239
If we get kicked out, we get kicked out.

112
00:07:02.240 --> 00:07:03.220
Oh, really?

113
00:07:03.910 --> 00:07:05.849
Then how are you going to make money?

114
00:07:05.850 --> 00:07:07.889
For us, who know nothing but fighting,

115
00:07:07.890 --> 00:07:09.520
how are we going to make money?

116
00:07:12.260 --> 00:07:14.070
Don't you just want to make easy money?

117
00:07:16.950 --> 00:07:18.710
Hey, f***. What do you even know?

118
00:07:22.640 --> 00:07:24.080
What don't I know?

119
00:07:25.110 --> 00:07:26.739
About the car you got for becoming part of the standing army,

120
00:07:26.740 --> 00:07:27.769
how you sold it but lost all the money gambling?

121
00:07:27.770 --> 00:07:29.299
Hey, you bastard.

122
00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:30.469
So you're the only clean one, huh?

123
00:07:30.470 --> 00:07:32.230
- Your grandpa... - Hey, damn it!

124
00:07:35.190 --> 00:07:36.340
What about my grandpa?

125
00:07:39.210 --> 00:07:40.190
F***.

126
00:07:53.270 --> 00:07:55.270
Are we going to keep letting that kid act so arrogant?

127
00:07:55.760 --> 00:07:56.620
Bang.

128
00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:11.650
Well, you must be feeling frustrated too.

129
00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:13.449
Because of your dad,

130
00:08:13.450 --> 00:08:15.489
you can't show off at school either.

131
00:08:15.490 --> 00:08:18.130
No wonder you feel a sense of similarity.

132
00:08:19.550 --> 00:08:21.359
So it's that teacher and that student.

133
00:08:21.360 --> 00:08:22.300
Exactly.

134
00:08:23.190 --> 00:08:24.320
Extremely interesting.

135
00:08:38.040 --> 00:08:38.950
What do you want?

136
00:08:39.530 --> 00:08:40.820
Didn't you say you wanted to protect them?

137
00:08:41.460 --> 00:08:43.040
Try it if you can.

138
00:08:45.910 --> 00:08:46.970
Hey, mister.

139
00:08:48.140 --> 00:08:49.920
I've been thinking,

140
00:08:52.680 --> 00:08:54.170
um, how about letting Sun-chul bro handle it?

141
00:09:08.430 --> 00:09:09.500
So,

142
00:09:10.180 --> 00:09:14.580
haven't you become an excellent person yet?

143
00:09:15.390 --> 00:09:17.339
Talking about becoming an excellent person again.

144
00:09:17.340 --> 00:09:19.189
You just asked yesterday.

145
00:09:19.190 --> 00:09:21.739
How can a person become excellent in just one day, Grandpa?

146
00:09:21.740 --> 00:09:23.970
My days left in this world are numbered.

147
00:09:24.440 --> 00:09:26.289
I'm anxious, you little brat.

148
00:09:26.290 --> 00:09:29.330
I need to see my grandson become an excellent person

149
00:09:29.710 --> 00:09:31.349
so I can die in peace.

150
00:09:31.350 --> 00:09:33.169
Looks like I'll have to become excellent slowly.

151
00:09:33.170 --> 00:09:35.130
That way, Grandpa can live a little longer.

152
00:09:35.740 --> 00:09:36.850
You brat.

153
00:09:38.200 --> 00:09:40.739
So please stop talking about dying all the time.

154
00:09:40.740 --> 00:09:42.370
You clearly have no intention of dying.

155
00:09:42.990 --> 00:09:45.100
Otherwise, why are you still studying for the TOEIC?

156
00:09:49.420 --> 00:09:53.740
Once a person stops learning,

157
00:09:57.130 --> 00:09:59.200
life also stops.

158
00:10:03.580 --> 00:10:05.930
You've always paid on time, what happened?

159
00:10:09.570 --> 00:10:10.570
I'm sorry.

160
00:10:11.010 --> 00:10:13.499
Please give me a little more time, I will quickly...

161
00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:14.370
I suppose so.

162
00:10:15.090 --> 00:10:16.380
It will indeed get harder and harder.

163
00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:18.660
You're a high school student, the expenses are not small.

164
00:10:22.010 --> 00:10:23.579
Anyway, for this time,

165
00:10:23.580 --> 00:10:25.050
I will help you figure something out.

166
00:10:25.680 --> 00:10:28.020
But it will be hard to delay again in the future, you know that right?

167
00:10:28.790 --> 00:10:30.020
Yes, thank you.

168
00:10:30.780 --> 00:10:31.640
Thank you.

169
00:10:33.260 --> 00:10:34.120
Thank you.

170
00:10:55.840 --> 00:10:56.830
What are you doing?

171
00:11:05.810 --> 00:11:08.460
I was wondering why you lunged at Pi Han-wool like that.

172
00:11:09.250 --> 00:11:10.630
So that's what happened.

173
00:11:14.230 --> 00:11:15.360
I'm sorry.

174
00:11:16.530 --> 00:11:17.930
I didn't know the situation was like that.

175
00:11:18.500 --> 00:11:19.560
It's fine.

176
00:11:21.540 --> 00:11:24.870
Is your mom... getting any better?

177
00:11:26.120 --> 00:11:26.980
Yes.

178
00:11:27.560 --> 00:11:29.630
The doctor said she can be discharged soon.

179
00:11:33.680 --> 00:11:34.690
That's a relief.

180
00:11:39.150 --> 00:11:40.090
But,

181
00:11:40.980 --> 00:11:43.050
why do you have to listen to Pi Han-wool?

182
00:11:47.080 --> 00:11:48.970
You want to study too, don't you?

183
00:12:03.230 --> 00:12:05.000
Can studying change anything?

184
00:12:05.780 --> 00:12:06.640
What?

185
00:12:08.700 --> 00:12:09.590
Well...

186
00:12:12.530 --> 00:12:14.420
- You can get into college. - And after getting into college?

187
00:12:18.450 --> 00:12:20.010
After getting into college, you can graduate.

188
00:12:20.430 --> 00:12:22.250
After graduating, you can find a good job, right?

189
00:12:22.860 --> 00:12:24.079
But,

190
00:12:24.080 --> 00:12:25.710
as long as I stay by Pi Han-wool's side,

191
00:12:26.600 --> 00:12:28.330
I can get into YB Construction.

192
00:12:29.040 --> 00:12:30.270
A well-known large corporation.

193
00:12:33.070 --> 00:12:34.540
I'm a senior in high school now.

194
00:12:36.030 --> 00:12:38.250
What can starting to study now change?

195
00:12:41.340 --> 00:12:42.250
(Dae-chul)

196
00:12:45.870 --> 00:12:47.250
Hey, Dae-chul.

197
00:12:47.610 --> 00:12:48.619
Hurry and find a place to hide.

198
00:12:48.620 --> 00:12:50.720
Those guys have shown up.

199
00:12:52.650 --> 00:12:53.510
The training supervisor?

200
00:12:53.511 --> 00:12:55.100
Yes, that's me.

201
00:12:58.090 --> 00:13:00.160
(Chae Sun-ho, Yeonbaek Gang Family, Standing Army Training Supervisor)

202
00:13:01.260 --> 00:13:04.070
(Kim Jae-seung, Yeonbaek Gang Family, Standing Army Training Supervisor)

203
00:13:06.240 --> 00:13:09.050
Sun-chul, long time no see.

204
00:13:11.500 --> 00:13:13.200
- Hello, you two. - Mm.

205
00:13:16.540 --> 00:13:17.970
Wow.

206
00:13:18.790 --> 00:13:20.870
You're looking well.

207
00:13:24.190 --> 00:13:25.910
You need to come with us.

208
00:13:27.720 --> 00:13:28.990
N-now?

209
00:13:31.360 --> 00:13:33.170
What's wrong? Not free?

210
00:13:34.660 --> 00:13:35.600
No, it's not that.

211
00:13:36.690 --> 00:13:38.060
Where are you guys going?

212
00:13:40.860 --> 00:13:41.870
Who's this?

213
00:13:45.070 --> 00:13:46.210
What's your name?

214
00:13:46.770 --> 00:13:47.670
Me?

215
00:13:48.270 --> 00:13:50.149
- I'm Yoon Jia... - I told you to get lost, you idiot.

216
00:13:50.150 --> 00:13:52.010
F***, where did this crazy kid come from?

217
00:13:54.250 --> 00:13:55.739
Looks like a freshman.

218
00:13:55.740 --> 00:13:56.820
I don't know him.

219
00:13:57.800 --> 00:13:58.660
Oh, really?

220
00:13:59.720 --> 00:14:01.170
This kid is interesting.

221
00:14:02.450 --> 00:14:03.730
Please lead the way.

222
00:14:04.280 --> 00:14:05.180
Let's go.

223
00:14:12.810 --> 00:14:14.050
Aren't you going to study?

224
00:14:14.640 --> 00:14:16.340
Midterms are coming up.

225
00:14:17.140 --> 00:14:19.189
Look at what that kid is saying to you.

226
00:14:19.190 --> 00:14:20.900
Something's wrong with his head.

227
00:14:21.440 --> 00:14:23.640
No wonder, he looks a bit stupid.

228
00:14:24.190 --> 00:14:25.269
Sun-chul.

229
00:14:25.270 --> 00:14:27.000
You have quite a lot to do today.

230
00:14:27.440 --> 00:14:29.180
It's going to be a long night.

231
00:14:45.640 --> 00:14:48.000
(Grandpa)

232
00:14:59.590 --> 00:15:00.590
I've checked them all.

233
00:15:01.170 --> 00:15:03.880
Okay, how many did I get wrong?

234
00:15:07.980 --> 00:15:09.049
4 questions.

235
00:15:09.050 --> 00:15:11.159
I only got 4 wrong?

236
00:15:11.160 --> 00:15:12.020
No.

237
00:15:12.420 --> 00:15:14.500
You got all of them wrong except for 4.

238
00:15:17.140 --> 00:15:19.579
But that's really amazing already!

239
00:15:19.580 --> 00:15:21.400
I don't even know a single one of these.

240
00:15:26.310 --> 00:15:28.029
Yesterday I only got 3 right.

241
00:15:28.030 --> 00:15:29.459
Today I got 1 more right!

242
00:15:29.460 --> 00:15:30.320
Let's see.

243
00:15:36.910 --> 00:15:39.189
Grandpa, why are you studying for the TOEIC?

244
00:15:39.190 --> 00:15:40.110
Why do you ask?

245
00:15:40.850 --> 00:15:41.780
Because,

246
00:15:42.320 --> 00:15:43.869
isn't the TOEIC only needed when looking for a job?

247
00:15:43.870 --> 00:15:46.079
So what you mean is,

248
00:15:46.080 --> 00:15:48.359
why is an old man who is about to die

249
00:15:48.360 --> 00:15:50.680
doing something so futile, right?

250
00:15:51.110 --> 00:15:52.040
No, that's not it...

251
00:15:52.990 --> 00:15:53.999
That's not what I meant.

252
00:15:54.000 --> 00:15:55.909
- It's fun. - What?

253
00:15:55.910 --> 00:15:59.629
Being able to become a better person every day than I was yesterday.

254
00:15:59.630 --> 00:16:03.540
How could I not do something so fun?

255
00:16:10.520 --> 00:16:11.600
Child.

256
00:16:13.980 --> 00:16:16.259
If you see our Sun-chul,

257
00:16:16.260 --> 00:16:20.929
tell him for me how fun studying is.

258
00:16:20.930 --> 00:16:23.730
I think you'll definitely be able to do it.

259
00:16:31.990 --> 00:16:32.610
Last night, around Ancheon Port,

260
00:16:32.611 --> 00:16:34.249
(Breaking News: Ancheon Port Knife Murder Case
Suspect is a teenage high school student)
Last night, around Ancheon Port,

261
00:16:34.250 --> 00:16:35.140
(Breaking News: Ancheon Port Knife Murder Case
Suspect is a teenage high school student)
a man in his 40s was found stabbed to death with a weapon.

262
00:16:35.141 --> 00:16:38.180
a man in his 40s was found stabbed to death with a weapon.

263
00:16:38.540 --> 00:16:40.509
The police used CCTV footage

264
00:16:40.510 --> 00:16:43.219
to identify the suspect as an 18-year-old student, Kim,

265
00:16:43.220 --> 00:16:45.659
(Breaking News: Ancheon Port Knife Murder Case
Suspect is a teenage high school student)
who attends a nearby high school,

266
00:16:45.660 --> 00:16:47.440
and are currently tracking his whereabouts.

267
00:16:48.120 --> 00:16:49.579
You can tell at a glance that's our school's uniform.

268
00:16:49.580 --> 00:16:51.519
But did he really kill someone?

269
00:16:51.520 --> 00:16:53.759
No, but I feel like I've seen him somewhere before.

270
00:16:53.760 --> 00:16:54.670
What?

271
00:16:54.671 --> 00:16:56.869
This blond hair, could it be Kim Sun-chul?

272
00:16:56.870 --> 00:16:58.839
- What? - Kim Sun-chul?

273
00:16:58.840 --> 00:17:00.459
- Yes. - Pi Han-wool's follower, Kim Sun-chul?

274
00:17:00.460 --> 00:17:01.320
Yes.

275
00:17:02.020 --> 00:17:03.119
You're right.

276
00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:04.979
Right? Yoon Jiamin, look at this.

277
00:17:04.980 --> 00:17:05.840
- Is it? - Yeah.

278
00:17:06.400 --> 00:17:08.599
- Look, this blond hair, it's him! - Yoon Jiamin!

279
00:17:08.600 --> 00:17:09.870
- It's Kim Sun-chul! - What's wrong with you?

280
00:17:14.090 --> 00:17:14.950
Nothing.

281
00:17:16.250 --> 00:17:18.119
But don't you guys think it really looks like him?

282
00:17:18.120 --> 00:17:19.450
Yeah, this blond hair, it's him.

283
00:17:23.260 --> 00:17:24.130
Yoon Jiamin.

284
00:17:24.790 --> 00:17:26.860
You met 3rd year Kim Sun-chul last night, didn't you?

285
00:17:34.750 --> 00:17:36.130
- Yes. - What?

286
00:17:38.130 --> 00:17:39.000
So you're saying,

287
00:17:39.380 --> 00:17:41.869
you guys were talking about studying,

288
00:17:41.870 --> 00:17:43.689
and then Kim Sun-chul met with Yeonbaek Gang members

289
00:17:43.690 --> 00:17:45.200
and left the hospital together.

290
00:17:46.710 --> 00:17:47.530
Yes.

291
00:17:47.531 --> 00:17:50.190
That was around 10:45 PM.

292
00:17:50.820 --> 00:17:51.680
Right.

293
00:17:53.700 --> 00:17:55.310
Is there anything else?

294
00:18:01.230 --> 00:18:04.269
Sun-chul, you have quite a lot to do today.

295
00:18:04.270 --> 00:18:05.600
It's going to be a long night.

296
00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:11.790
No, nothing else.

297
00:18:18.320 --> 00:18:20.710
Alright, I understand.

298
00:18:23.170 --> 00:18:24.230
But,

299
00:18:25.340 --> 00:18:26.200
yes?

300
00:18:27.340 --> 00:18:28.220
Excuse me...

301
00:18:30.640 --> 00:18:34.539
do you really think Sun-chul bro is a murderer?

302
00:18:34.540 --> 00:18:37.189
As of right now, he is the prime suspect.

303
00:18:37.190 --> 00:18:38.050
No.

304
00:18:38.810 --> 00:18:41.199
I'm asking if you really think so too.

305
00:18:41.200 --> 00:18:43.370
Hey, do my thoughts matter?

306
00:18:44.010 --> 00:18:45.640
The current situation is what it is.

307
00:19:03.930 --> 00:19:05.250
Are you still thinking about that?

308
00:19:06.160 --> 00:19:07.120
But,

309
00:19:08.550 --> 00:19:10.890
would Sun-chul bro really do something like that?

310
00:19:12.420 --> 00:19:13.789
He is a member of the standing army after all.

311
00:19:13.790 --> 00:19:15.410
And he's also very close with Pi Han-wool.

312
00:19:17.580 --> 00:19:18.550
But...

313
00:19:18.551 --> 00:19:20.670
What's wrong? You don't think it's him?

314
00:19:36.120 --> 00:19:38.140
What's going on, waking people up so early in the morning?

315
00:19:38.720 --> 00:19:42.339
Hee-won and I investigated the Kim Sun-chul case.

316
00:19:42.340 --> 00:19:43.900
I was wondering what it was about.

317
00:19:44.510 --> 00:19:45.769
Hey, why are you doing this too?

318
00:19:45.770 --> 00:19:48.969
Whatever trouble those delinquent thugs stir up has nothing to do with us, right?

319
00:19:48.970 --> 00:19:49.850
Right.

320
00:19:53.590 --> 00:19:54.450
Look at this.

321
00:19:55.430 --> 00:19:57.949
Here, look closely at this chart.

322
00:19:57.950 --> 00:19:59.789
(Increase in Juvenile Crime in Yeonseo District)
Starting last year, when Pi Han-wool enrolled,

323
00:19:59.790 --> 00:20:03.300
the number of murders committed by high school students in the Ancheon area suddenly increased.

324
00:20:04.190 --> 00:20:06.620
There is a much more significant difference compared to other areas.

325
00:20:07.440 --> 00:20:08.850
Is this a crime hotspot?

326
00:20:09.480 --> 00:20:11.199
But looking at it this way,

327
00:20:11.200 --> 00:20:13.660
the overall crime rate is almost the same as other areas.

328
00:20:14.140 --> 00:20:16.130
What does that mean? Explain it more simply.

329
00:20:16.510 --> 00:20:18.409
The overall crime rate is the same,

330
00:20:18.410 --> 00:20:20.059
only the juvenile crime rate has increased.

331
00:20:20.060 --> 00:20:22.689
This means adult crime rate has actually decreased,

332
00:20:22.690 --> 00:20:24.939
while high school student crime is increasing.

333
00:20:24.940 --> 00:20:25.940
In other words,

334
00:20:25.941 --> 00:20:29.339
high school students are being used for adult crimes.

335
00:20:29.340 --> 00:20:30.840
We can think of it that way, right?

336
00:20:31.420 --> 00:20:32.890
High school students being used?

337
00:20:33.980 --> 00:20:34.850
Why?

338
00:20:35.240 --> 00:20:37.489
What advantages do we have over those gangster misters?

339
00:20:37.490 --> 00:20:39.460
- Looks? - Bingo.

340
00:20:39.960 --> 00:20:40.820
Hee-won.

341
00:20:41.220 --> 00:20:42.459
Ah, sorry.

342
00:20:42.460 --> 00:20:44.110
I thought that answer wasn't wrong either.

343
00:20:46.380 --> 00:20:47.240
Age?

344
00:20:48.090 --> 00:20:49.140
Bingo.

345
00:20:50.980 --> 00:20:52.469
Psycho four-eyes, when did you get here?

346
00:20:52.470 --> 00:20:54.080
I just got goosebumps.

347
00:20:55.130 --> 00:20:55.990
Exactly.

348
00:20:56.380 --> 00:20:58.189
Because we are all minors,

349
00:20:58.190 --> 00:21:00.049
the Juvenile Act applies to us.

350
00:21:00.050 --> 00:21:01.450
A minor who is a first-time offender

351
00:21:01.840 --> 00:21:04.030
can be released on parole in just a few years.

352
00:21:12.140 --> 00:21:13.369
Seriously.

353
00:21:13.370 --> 00:21:15.149
They actually murdered someone,

354
00:21:15.150 --> 00:21:16.370
and they only get locked up for a few years?

355
00:21:17.930 --> 00:21:20.399
What are you guys doing, directing and acting in your own play?

356
00:21:20.400 --> 00:21:22.710
I thought you guys would ask,

357
00:21:24.540 --> 00:21:26.670
even so, would they willingly take the fall and go to jail?

358
00:21:27.570 --> 00:21:28.640
Hmm...

359
00:21:29.510 --> 00:21:31.249
If they go to jail for about three years,

360
00:21:31.250 --> 00:21:33.659
they can become members of the Yeonbaek Gang when they get out,
and even become employees of YB Construction.

361
00:21:33.660 --> 00:21:35.980
Oh, that's a huge profit.

362
00:21:36.620 --> 00:21:38.100
Hey, how can you say that?

363
00:21:39.250 --> 00:21:41.359
Okay, even if that's true,

364
00:21:41.360 --> 00:21:43.960
where is the evidence that that delinquent isn't the murderer?

365
00:21:44.970 --> 00:21:45.890
Hmm...

366
00:21:48.120 --> 00:21:49.160
There is no evidence.

367
00:22:09.050 --> 00:22:10.449
Please help me.

368
00:22:10.450 --> 00:22:12.329
Oh, you're Sun-chul bro's friend.

369
00:22:12.330 --> 00:22:14.320
Sun-chul is not the culprit.

370
00:22:15.680 --> 00:22:17.780
What bullshit are you saying, bastard?

371
00:22:18.320 --> 00:22:19.280
Hey, Dae-chul.

372
00:22:20.200 --> 00:22:23.169
Our Dae-chul is still spouting nonsense.

373
00:22:23.170 --> 00:22:24.830
Looks like you need a bit more education.

374
00:22:30.170 --> 00:22:31.250
The education you speak of,

375
00:22:31.880 --> 00:22:33.620
doesn't mean studying together, does it?

376
00:22:35.970 --> 00:22:37.610
What is this psycho talking about?

377
00:22:39.130 --> 00:22:40.769
Oh.

378
00:22:40.770 --> 00:22:43.280
Aren't you that ugly psycho from the hospital back then?

379
00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:51.340
No.

380
00:22:54.040 --> 00:22:55.649
Look at this guy.

381
00:22:55.650 --> 00:22:56.510
Hey.

382
00:22:57.530 --> 00:22:59.800
What are you trying to do, glaring at me like that? Speak up!

383
00:23:01.460 --> 00:23:02.540
Just keep walking your path.

384
00:23:06.390 --> 00:23:08.189
My goodness, both of them are acting crazy here.

385
00:23:08.190 --> 00:23:09.390
A bunch of bastards.

386
00:23:10.370 --> 00:23:12.060
From now on, you brought this upon yourself.

387
00:23:22.350 --> 00:23:24.829
You despicable guy...

388
00:23:24.830 --> 00:23:26.750
Iron pipe... no, iron ball...

389
00:23:34.500 --> 00:23:35.690
What is going on here?

390
00:23:44.770 --> 00:23:46.160
I saw it clearly.

391
00:23:46.720 --> 00:23:47.770
Choo Sung-woong...

392
00:23:49.180 --> 00:23:50.990
was washing a bloody knife at the time.

393
00:23:53.450 --> 00:23:57.459
Actually, among the standing army, this is an open secret.

394
00:23:57.460 --> 00:23:59.390
If a Yeonbaek Gang executive kills someone,

395
00:24:00.490 --> 00:24:02.450
the standing army takes the fall and goes to jail for them.

396
00:24:06.260 --> 00:24:07.660
Do you believe that story?

397
00:24:09.610 --> 00:24:11.929
Although I unconditionally believe whatever God Jiamin says...

398
00:24:11.930 --> 00:24:13.450
Even I find this a bit...

399
00:24:14.430 --> 00:24:16.739
Wake up, you naive fool.

400
00:24:16.740 --> 00:24:18.960
Those thugs are using you!

401
00:24:20.200 --> 00:24:22.340
Ah, is that so?

402
00:24:25.310 --> 00:24:26.880
But Sun-chul bro...

403
00:24:34.680 --> 00:24:37.120
His eyes clearly showed he wanted to study.

404
00:24:43.390 --> 00:24:44.510
Then you have to believe him.

405
00:24:46.870 --> 00:24:47.830
Yeah.

406
00:24:47.830 --> 00:24:48.790
Me too.

407
00:24:56.280 --> 00:24:57.690
Just based on those eyes...

408
00:25:01.220 --> 00:25:02.570
Of course I believe him.

409
00:25:06.480 --> 00:25:08.139
From the very beginning,

410
00:25:08.140 --> 00:25:09.390
I believed Sun-chul bro.

411
00:25:10.070 --> 00:25:11.619
Since when did you start calling him Sun-chul bro?

412
00:25:11.620 --> 00:25:13.439
You used to call him Kim Sun-chul.

413
00:25:13.440 --> 00:25:14.430
Do you think I'm you?

414
00:25:14.431 --> 00:25:16.510
Hey, your wings have grown hard, huh?

415
00:25:17.480 --> 00:25:18.480
However,

416
00:25:18.850 --> 00:25:20.240
If that's the case now,

417
00:25:21.070 --> 00:25:22.540
what should we do?

418
00:25:32.280 --> 00:25:33.460
But that knife,

419
00:25:34.140 --> 00:25:36.249
if they were going to throw it away, they wouldn't have washed it.

420
00:25:36.250 --> 00:25:37.719
(YB Group Talent Development Center)

421
00:25:37.720 --> 00:25:39.730
We just need to find the murderer's knife there, right?

422
00:25:40.790 --> 00:25:42.640
Pull yourselves together.

423
00:25:49.430 --> 00:25:50.670
Be careful not to get hurt.

424
00:25:51.530 --> 00:25:52.530
Thank you.

425
00:25:53.260 --> 00:25:56.519
And it seems Seo Yoo-bi hasn't reformed yet.

426
00:25:56.520 --> 00:25:58.360
If you run into him, teach him a good lesson.

427
00:26:00.890 --> 00:26:02.179
Calling base.

428
00:26:02.180 --> 00:26:03.290
Can you hear me clearly? Over.

429
00:26:04.840 --> 00:26:05.979
Really getting into it.

430
00:26:05.980 --> 00:26:06.840
Yeah.

431
00:26:08.130 --> 00:26:09.809
This is base.

432
00:26:09.810 --> 00:26:11.050
Hearing you loud and clear. Over.

433
00:26:12.020 --> 00:26:14.200
We won't get caught right at the entrance, will we?

434
00:26:15.470 --> 00:26:18.309
There are more than just a few people in the standing army,
they probably don't even know all the faces, right?

435
00:26:18.310 --> 00:26:19.739
Yeah, don't worry.

436
00:26:19.740 --> 00:26:22.550
If we feel we're in danger, we'll call the police immediately.

437
00:26:24.060 --> 00:26:24.920
Let's go.

438
00:26:41.130 --> 00:26:41.990
Names.

439
00:26:43.600 --> 00:26:44.950
Heukchang High School, Gook Gwan-woo.

440
00:26:45.780 --> 00:26:46.999
I'm Jang Bi-hwan.

441
00:26:47.000 --> 00:26:49.270
Seo Yoo-bi.

442
00:26:51.610 --> 00:26:53.140
All unfamiliar faces.

443
00:26:59.770 --> 00:27:01.959
Gook Gwan-woo, Jang Bi-hwan,

444
00:27:01.960 --> 00:27:03.240
Seo Yoo-bi.

445
00:27:05.180 --> 00:27:06.580
From Heukchang High School.

446
00:27:09.160 --> 00:27:10.820
Alright, go on in.

447
00:27:14.500 --> 00:27:15.720
Thank you.

448
00:27:18.600 --> 00:27:19.510
Oh yeah!

449
00:27:22.630 --> 00:27:24.059
But Kim Se-hyun, you bastard.

450
00:27:24.060 --> 00:27:25.650
How could they not recognize our faces? Damn it.

451
00:27:26.580 --> 00:27:27.440
Sorry.

452
00:27:29.580 --> 00:27:30.650
Thank goodness.

453
00:27:31.160 --> 00:27:33.079
I thought we were going to get caught, I was so scared.

454
00:27:33.080 --> 00:27:35.120
We worried for nothing. What a bunch of idiots.

455
00:27:35.660 --> 00:27:37.380
Are there girls in the standing army too?

456
00:27:40.980 --> 00:27:42.000
Probably.

457
00:27:44.850 --> 00:27:45.950
You guys wait a second.

458
00:27:47.370 --> 00:27:48.230
We're doomed.

459
00:27:48.860 --> 00:27:49.720
What are you doing?

460
00:27:50.550 --> 00:27:51.500
Glasses.

461
00:27:58.390 --> 00:28:00.630
- What's wrong? - Did you say your name was Gook Gwan-woo?

462
00:28:02.940 --> 00:28:03.800
Yes.

463
00:28:04.160 --> 00:28:05.060
Are we busted?

464
00:28:05.061 --> 00:28:06.560
I told you not to wear glasses.

465
00:28:10.760 --> 00:28:12.300
Are you guys here for cram school or something?

466
00:28:13.150 --> 00:28:14.430
Why did you come with backpacks?

467
00:28:15.680 --> 00:28:17.049
You better tighten up your attitude.

468
00:28:17.050 --> 00:28:18.760
Hey, I was just about to say the same thing.

469
00:28:19.850 --> 00:28:21.329
You little brats, get inside quickly.

470
00:28:21.330 --> 00:28:22.190
Yes, sir.

471
00:28:25.900 --> 00:28:26.850
Seriously.

472
00:28:27.960 --> 00:28:28.820
Hey.

473
00:28:29.890 --> 00:28:31.120
Sorry.

474
00:28:31.550 --> 00:28:32.870
It is exam week after all.

475
00:28:51.190 --> 00:28:52.050
Huh?

476
00:28:53.750 --> 00:28:55.530
Is today some kind of big day?

477
00:28:56.510 --> 00:28:57.370
What's wrong?

478
00:28:57.930 --> 00:28:58.880
Did we mess up?

479
00:29:04.290 --> 00:29:05.080
Hey, but...

480
00:29:05.081 --> 00:29:07.590
isn't the standing army supposed to gather for a general meeting soon?

481
00:29:08.260 --> 00:29:09.170
Oh yeah.

482
00:29:12.460 --> 00:29:14.320
But it can't possibly be today.

483
00:29:15.140 --> 00:29:17.560
Gook Gwan-woo and Jang Bi-hwan are total bastards.

484
00:29:18.380 --> 00:29:20.679
Hey, this feels like it's going to be really dangerous.

485
00:29:20.680 --> 00:29:21.839
- You guys should just leave. - Yeah.

486
00:29:21.840 --> 00:29:24.070
This is too dangerous.

487
00:29:24.820 --> 00:29:26.460
No way. Since we're already here,

488
00:29:26.920 --> 00:29:28.609
let's find the thing as quickly as possible and then leave.

489
00:29:28.610 --> 00:29:29.629
I agree.

490
00:29:29.630 --> 00:29:30.889
I'm too lazy to come here again.

491
00:29:30.890 --> 00:29:31.770
But...

492
00:29:59.450 --> 00:30:01.879
- Hee-won, can you fly over to the left and take a look? - Yeah.

493
00:30:01.880 --> 00:30:02.970
Of course.

494
00:30:06.120 --> 00:30:07.990
- Looks like there's someone there. - Yeah.

495
00:30:08.800 --> 00:30:11.279
Pi Han-wool and Choo Sung-woong are on the fourth floor.

496
00:30:11.280 --> 00:30:12.449
Those two are staying together.

497
00:30:12.450 --> 00:30:13.589
Pi Han-wool?

498
00:30:13.590 --> 00:30:15.579
Why is that guy here again?

499
00:30:15.580 --> 00:30:17.049
You guys wait a minute.

500
00:30:17.050 --> 00:30:18.859
Because the knife is probably there.

501
00:30:18.860 --> 00:30:20.520
You guys wait for them to leave first.

502
00:30:26.080 --> 00:30:27.330
We're on the fourth floor now. Over.

503
00:30:29.160 --> 00:30:31.540
Oh, they're getting up. Get ready.

504
00:30:43.870 --> 00:30:44.960
They came out.

505
00:30:45.990 --> 00:30:47.840
Just wait for those guys to take the elevator downstairs...

506
00:30:48.580 --> 00:30:49.440
Huh?

507
00:30:50.660 --> 00:30:51.520
What's wrong?

508
00:30:52.990 --> 00:30:53.920
Damn it.

509
00:30:56.890 --> 00:30:58.329
- What's wrong? - What?

510
00:30:58.330 --> 00:30:59.679
Why are those guys heading this way?

511
00:30:59.680 --> 00:31:02.349
Why aren't they taking the perfectly good elevator and coming this way instead?

512
00:31:02.350 --> 00:31:03.210
What did you say?

513
00:31:05.380 --> 00:31:08.229
Sun-chul bro said he will turn himself in
after the general meeting today.

514
00:31:08.230 --> 00:31:09.340
I'm just letting you know beforehand.

515
00:31:09.870 --> 00:31:10.730
Yes.

516
00:31:18.710 --> 00:31:20.270
Get the elevator fixed quickly.

517
00:31:22.530 --> 00:31:23.410
Sorry.

518
00:31:31.530 --> 00:31:32.390
What's wrong?

519
00:31:34.230 --> 00:31:36.560
I thought I heard a door closing on the roof.

520
00:31:39.660 --> 00:31:41.629
Who would go to the roof at this hour?

521
00:31:41.630 --> 00:31:42.490
Hurry and follow.

522
00:31:43.020 --> 00:31:44.159
But just in case,

523
00:31:44.160 --> 00:31:45.790
I'll go check and follow you right away.

524
00:31:52.030 --> 00:31:53.409
Not the roof, the second floor.

525
00:31:53.410 --> 00:31:54.640
You idiots.

526
00:31:55.150 --> 00:31:56.719
Wait for them to go down to the first floor,

527
00:31:56.720 --> 00:31:58.990
and we'll immediately go upstairs. Got it?

528
00:32:01.670 --> 00:32:02.530
Huh?

529
00:32:04.840 --> 00:32:06.100
Damn it, what's going on?

530
00:32:06.500 --> 00:32:07.440
Damn it.

531
00:32:07.870 --> 00:32:09.099
Hey, Yoon Jiamin.

532
00:32:09.100 --> 00:32:10.630
Where did you run off to now?

533
00:33:16.310 --> 00:33:17.170
Huh?

534
00:33:24.220 --> 00:33:25.240
Is it locked?

535
00:33:26.250 --> 00:33:29.720
(Deputy: Kim Sun-chul)

536
00:33:35.590 --> 00:33:36.450
Hey...

537
00:33:42.050 --> 00:33:45.050
(Standing Army Regular General Meeting)

538
00:33:57.050 --> 00:33:58.030
Sun-chul bro.

539
00:34:22.730 --> 00:34:24.800
Sun-chul bro has become part of our family.

540
00:34:27.180 --> 00:34:31.020
(Standing Army Regular General Meeting)

541
00:34:50.670 --> 00:34:52.050
This is for clothing expenses.

542
00:34:52.990 --> 00:34:55.350
You can use it to help with your grandpa's medical bills, right?

543
00:35:07.980 --> 00:35:10.309
Everyone, don't just stand there being envious.

544
00:35:10.310 --> 00:35:11.750
You should be congratulating him.

545
00:35:27.120 --> 00:35:29.369
- Why is Jiamin there? - Damn it.

546
00:35:29.370 --> 00:35:30.910
Hey, Yoon Jiamin, think of something!

547
00:35:31.290 --> 00:35:32.909
But...

548
00:35:32.910 --> 00:35:34.430
the door won't open at all.

549
00:35:35.320 --> 00:35:37.600
You probably need to get in quickly now.

550
00:35:38.180 --> 00:35:40.570
Then why didn't you follow us instead of going to the roof by yourself?

551
00:35:42.210 --> 00:35:43.070
Sorry.

552
00:35:43.610 --> 00:35:45.159
Don't you worry.

553
00:35:45.160 --> 00:35:47.030
I'll just take over God Jiamin's mission!

554
00:35:47.830 --> 00:35:49.470
Damn it, I'm really going to go crazy.

555
00:35:49.830 --> 00:35:50.870
Since it's come to this...

556
00:35:51.800 --> 00:35:52.660
Huh?

557
00:35:57.030 --> 00:35:57.890
Wait.

558
00:35:58.250 --> 00:35:59.270
What is it now?

559
00:36:00.460 --> 00:36:02.390
Those guys who went in with backpacks earlier,

560
00:36:02.780 --> 00:36:04.669
were they named Gook Gwan-woo, Jang Bi-hwan, and Seo Yoo-bi?

561
00:36:04.670 --> 00:36:06.439
Yeah, so what?

562
00:36:06.440 --> 00:36:08.220
Didn't he go in by himself earlier?

563
00:36:09.160 --> 00:36:10.040
Seo Yoo-bi.

564
00:36:13.490 --> 00:36:15.379
Why is today so unlucky?

565
00:36:15.380 --> 00:36:18.019
Why is that guy appearing here now?

566
00:36:18.020 --> 00:36:19.220
Don't worry, Ji-woo.

567
00:36:20.030 --> 00:36:21.150
You know what I mean, right?

568
00:36:24.580 --> 00:36:26.830
I'll let it slide that you tried to act cool today.

569
00:36:27.650 --> 00:36:29.300
Just hold out as long as you can.

570
00:36:30.560 --> 00:36:32.170
I told you not to worry.

571
00:36:35.670 --> 00:36:36.530
Lee Ji-woo.

572
00:36:47.450 --> 00:36:48.610
Joon, be careful.

573
00:36:49.130 --> 00:36:51.900
It's bad enough you guys get startled seeing me,

574
00:36:52.510 --> 00:36:55.139
but wearing our school's uniform too?

575
00:36:55.140 --> 00:36:57.620
Back then you pretended to be the number one ranker,

576
00:36:58.950 --> 00:37:01.150
are you pretending to be the standing army now?

577
00:37:01.720 --> 00:37:02.859
You're very observant.

578
00:37:02.860 --> 00:37:05.539
Haven't you woken up yet after getting crushed by me back then?

579
00:37:05.540 --> 00:37:06.609
Damn it.

580
00:37:06.610 --> 00:37:09.690
It was 3 against 1 back then, you can't really call it getting crushed.

581
00:37:10.140 --> 00:37:11.289
Also,

582
00:37:11.290 --> 00:37:13.169
the one who needs to wake up isn't me, it's you.

583
00:37:13.170 --> 00:37:15.210
Are you crazy, you strawberry head? Damn it.

584
00:37:16.660 --> 00:37:18.820
Today, with the mindset of saving a life,

585
00:37:19.360 --> 00:37:20.480
I'll do that for you.

586
00:37:21.220 --> 00:37:22.220
Ah, what was it called again?

587
00:37:23.570 --> 00:37:24.660
Damn it...

588
00:37:28.260 --> 00:37:29.549
You can do it! You can do it!

589
00:37:29.550 --> 00:37:31.070
Rehabilitated person!

590
00:37:31.470 --> 00:37:32.430
- Hee-won. - What?

591
00:37:33.670 --> 00:37:35.350
- There... - What...

592
00:37:36.280 --> 00:37:37.140
That person.

593
00:37:39.560 --> 00:37:40.420
Huh?

594
00:37:44.200 --> 00:37:45.729
Detective Na Tae-man is here.

595
00:37:45.730 --> 00:37:46.829
We have to move faster.

596
00:37:46.830 --> 00:37:48.530
We have to be fast before Sun-chul bro is arrested.

597
00:37:54.590 --> 00:37:55.600
Damn it.

598
00:38:00.300 --> 00:38:01.160
Damn it.

599
00:38:09.760 --> 00:38:10.889
Lee Ji-woo, did you find it?

600
00:38:10.890 --> 00:38:12.170
Haven't found it yet.

601
00:38:31.050 --> 00:38:31.910
Found it.

602
00:38:32.840 --> 00:38:33.700
Found it?

603
00:38:34.150 --> 00:38:35.279
If you found it, come out quickly.

604
00:38:35.280 --> 00:38:36.730
Ji-woo, hurry!

605
00:39:08.100 --> 00:39:10.030
Lee Ji-woo. Lee Ji-woo!

606
00:39:10.490 --> 00:39:11.120
Ji-woo!

607
00:39:11.121 --> 00:39:13.320
Why isn't Ji-woo answering suddenly?

608
00:40:17.840 --> 00:40:18.700
Is it a girl?

609
00:40:21.140 --> 00:40:22.590
She's pretty cute.

610
00:40:25.010 --> 00:40:26.630
I killed someone.

611
00:40:44.080 --> 00:40:45.360
What the hell is this now?

612
00:40:56.670 --> 00:41:00.710
"Study Group"

613
00:42:06.770 --> 00:42:15.080
